{#
  Self-hosted OBSIDIAN type families. The @font-face rules live in the theme CSS
  (web/css/theme.source.css) and are served from our own origin via Vite — no
  Google Fonts round-trip, no preconnects. font-display:swap keeps text visible
  meanwhile.

  All three are preloaded: they carry the hero LCP and the bulk of the page's
  text, and their swap is what reflows the layout — waiting for the stylesheet to
  request them puts that reflow half a second in. Mono is no exception in
  practice: it dresses the demo bar, the header actions and the hero eyebrow, all
  above the fold, so discovering it from the stylesheet repainted half the
  viewport a second late.
#}
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ block.getViteFileUrl('bodoni-moda-latin-wght-normal.woff2') }}">
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ block.getViteFileUrl('hanken-grotesk-latin-wght-normal.woff2') }}">
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ block.getViteFileUrl('jetbrains-mono-latin-wght-normal.woff2') }}">
